        <mxCell id="c238" value="&lt;b&gt;The action plans&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;sheet Report&lt;/i&gt;" style="rounded=0;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E8F6F3;strokeColor=#117A65;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#2C3E50;fontSize=12;fontStyle=0;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="671.99" y="360" width="168" height="44" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c239" value="&lt;i&gt;The page limits are the case&#x27;s: a report of no more than three pages and an appendix of no more than three. Page 2&#x27;s table has the six elements of a finding (condition, criteria, cause, effect, rating, recommendation) for each of the model answer&#x27;s 6 findings; page 3&#x27;s has an action, an owner by role, a date, the response expected and where disagreement is expected with the evidence that answers it. The six exhibits of the appendix are the workbook&#x27;s own sheets; the model answer&#x27;s text (the conclusion, findings, clean results and action plans) runs to about 1,854 words. Pages are not to scale.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="472" width="860" height="68" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
